{"name":"Pickled Beets","hex":"#aa0044","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pickled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of pickle"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Preserved by pickling.","Drunk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pickled"},{"term":"beets","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of beet"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beets"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pickling","blocks":[{"text":"Pickling is the process of preserving or extending the shelf life of food by either anaerobic fermentation in brine or immersion in vinegar. The pickling procedure typically affects the food's texture and flavor. The resulting food is called a pickle, or, if named, the name is prefaced with the word \"pickled\". Foods that are pickled include vegetables, fruits, mushrooms, meats, fish, dairy and eggs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Gherkins_and_Onions.JPG/330px-Gherkins_and_Onions.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pickling","wikidata":"Q1503967"},{"title":"Beetroot","blocks":[{"text":"Beetroot or beet is the taproot portion of a Beta vulgaris subsp. vulgaris plant in the Conditiva Group. The plant is a root vegetable also known as the table beet, garden beet, or dinner beet, or else categorized by color as red beet or golden beet. Its leaves constitute a leaf vegetable called beet greens. It is native to the Azores, Western Europe to the Mediterranean and India.\nBeetroot can be eaten raw, roasted, steamed, or boiled. Beetroot can also be canned, either whole or cut up, and often are pickled, spiced, or served in a sweet-and-sour sauce."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Detroitdarkredbeets.png/330px-Detroitdarkredbeets.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beetroot","wikidata":"Q165437"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg/500px-Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg/500px-Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Torshi, traditional pickles in Southeast Europe, West Asia and Northern Africa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG/1280px-PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kosher torshi in Israel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Indian-pickle.jpg/500px-Indian-pickle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Indian-pickle.jpg/500px-Indian-pickle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Indian mixed pickle, containing lotus root, lemon, carrot, green mango, green chilis, and other ingredients","link":"h